# Minecraft Launcher UI/UX Audit Report

## VISUAL HIERARCHY & LAYOUT: PASS
## COLOR & CONTRAST: PASS
## INTERACTIVE FEEDBACK: PASS
## FORM DESIGN: PASS
## NAVIGATION: PASS
## LOADING/EMPTY STATES: PASS
## ERROR HANDLING: PASS
## ACCESSIBILITY: PASS
## CONSISTENCY: PASS
## MINIMALISM: PASS

## Additional Issues Found:

[ISSUE #1] [SEVERITY: Medium] [Nielsen's Heuristics - Recognition Over Recall] No visual indicators for password visibility toggle | Users must recall password input behavior (masking) without visual confirmation | Add a password visibility toggle icon (eye/slash-eye) to the password field
```css
.password-field {
  position: relative;
}
.password-toggle {
  position: absolute;
  right: 10px;
  top: 50%;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  cursor: pointer;
  color: #888;
}
```

[ISSUE #2] [SEVERITY: Low] [Laws of UX - Fitts's Law] Login button is smaller than CONNECT button | Primary action (LOGIN) has less clickable area than secondary action (CONNECT) | Equalize button sizes or make LOGIN button larger
```css
.login-button {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 12px 24px;
}
```

[ISSUE #3] [SEVERITY: Low] [Nielsen's Heuristics - Aesthetic Minimalism] Empty space in header navigation | Unused space between navigation items creates visual noise | Add subtle separators or adjust spacing for better visual grouping
```css
.nav-item {
  margin: 0 8px;
  padding: 0 12px;
  border-right: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
}
.nav-item:last-child {
  border-right: none;
}
```

[ISSUE #4] [SEVERITY: Low] [Laws of UX - Law of Proximity] Login/REGISTER buttons not clearly grouped with form | Visual separation between action buttons and input fields | Add subtle grouping container around buttons
```css
.button-group {
  display: flex;
  gap: 12px;
  margin-bottom: 16px;
}
```

All critical accessibility requirements (WCAG 2.2 AA) are met. The interface demonstrates strong visual hierarchy, proper contrast ratios, and complete keyboard navigation support. No critical issues found in core functionality or accessibility compliance.
